            <ArticleTitle>Suprasellar arachnoid cyst diagnosed preoperatively by computerized tomographic scanning.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>299-303</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>True arachnoid cysts of the suprasellar region are uncommon and have rarely been diagnosed pre-operatively. An histologically verified suprasellar arachnoid cyst producing hydrocephalus and visual loss in a 19-year-old man was diagnosed by a combination of pneumoencephalography and computerized tomographic (CT) scanning prior to surgery. The incidence, pathogenesis, signs, and treatment of suprasellar arachnoid cysts are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
